ne (own), my"},"G3451":{"lemma":"μουσικός","xlit":"mousikós","derivation":"from (a Muse);","def":"\"musical\", i.e. (as noun) a minstrel","kjv":"musician"},"G3452":{"lemma":"μυελός","xlit":"myelós","derivation":"perhaps a primary word;","def":"the marrow","kjv":"marrow"},"G3453":{"lemma":"μυέω","xlit":"myéō","derivation":"from the base of G3466 (μυστήριον);","def":"to initiate, i.e. (by implication) to teach","kjv":"instruct"},"G3454":{"lemma":"μῦθος","xlit":"mŷthos","derivation":"perhaps from the same as G3453 (μυέω) (through the idea of tuition);","def":"a tale, i.e. fiction (\"myth\")","kjv":"fable"},"G3455":{"lemma":"μυκάομαι","xlit":"mykáomai","derivation":"from a presumed derivative of ( to \"moo\");","def":"to bellow (roar)","kjv":"roar"},"G3456":{"lemma":"μυκτηρίζω","xlit":"myktērízō","derivation":"from a derivative of the base of G3455 (μυκάομαι) (meaning snout, as that whence lowing proceeds);","def":"to make mouths at, i.e. ridicule","kjv":"mock"},"G3457":{"lemma":"μυλικός","xlit":"mylikós","derivation":"from G3458 (μύλος);","def":"belonging to a mill","kjv":"mill(-stone)"},"G3458":{"lemma":"μύλος","xlit":"mýlos","derivation":"probably ultimately from the base of G3433 (μόλις) (through the idea of hardship);","def":"a \"mill\", i.e. (by implication), a grinder (millstone)","kjv":"millstone"},"G3459":{"lemma":"μύλων","xlit":"mýlōn","derivation":"from G3458 (μύλος);","def":"a mill-house","kjv":"mill"},"G3460":{"lemma":"Μύρα","xlit":"Mýra","derivation":"of uncertain derivation;","def":"Myra, a place in Asia Minor","kjv":"Myra"},"G3461":{"lemma":"μυριάς","xlit":"myriás","derivation":"from G3463 (μύριοι);","def":"a ten-thousand; by extension, a \"myriad\" or indefinite number","kjv":"ten thousand"},"G3462":{"lemma":"μυρίζω","xlit":"myrízō","derivation":"from G3464 (μύρον);","def":"to apply (perfumed) unguent to","kjv":"anoint"},"G3463":{"lemma":"μύριοι","xlit":"mýrioi","derivation":"plural of an apparently primary word (properly, meaning very many);","def":"ten thousand; by extension, innumerably many","kjv":"ten thousand"},"G3464":{"lemma":"μύρον","xlit":"mýron","derivation":"probably of foreign origin (compare H04753, G4666 (σμύρνα));","def":"\"myrrh\", i.e. (by implication) perfumed oil","kjv":"ointment"},"G3465":{"lemma":"Μυσία","xlit":"Mysía","derivation":"of uncertain origin;","def":"Mysia, a region of Asia Minor","kjv":"Mysia"},"G3466":{"lemma":"μυστήριον","xlit":"mystḗrion","derivation":"from a derivative of (to shut the mouth);","def":"a secret or \"mystery\" (through the idea of silence imposed by initiation into religious rites)","kjv":"mystery"},"G3467":{"lemma":"μυωπάζω","xlit":"myōpázō","derivation":"from a compound of the base of G3466 (μυστήριον) and (the face;","def":"from G3700 (ὀπτάνομαι)); to shut the eyes, i.e. blink (see indistinctly)","kjv":"cannot see far off"},"G3468":{"lemma":"μώλωψ","xlit":"mṓlōps","derivation":"from (\"moil\";","def":"probably akin to the base of G3433 (μόλις)) and probably (the face; from G3700 (ὀπτάνομαι)); a mole (\"black eye\") or blow-mark","kjv":"stripe"},"G3469":{"lemma":"μωμάομαι","xlit":"mōmáomai","derivation":"from G3470 (μῶμος);","def":"to carp at, i.e. censure (discredit)","kjv":"blame"},"G3470":{"lemma":"μῶμος","xlit":"mōmos","derivation":"perhaps from G3201 (μέμφομαι);","def":"a flaw or blot, i.e. (figuratively) disgraceful person","kjv":"blemish"},"G3471":{"lemma":"μωραίνω","xlit":"mōraínō","derivation":"from G3474 (μωρός);","def":"to become insipid; figuratively, to make (passively, act) as a simpleton","kjv":"become fool, make foolish, lose savour"},"G3472":{"lemma":"μωρία","xlit":"mōría","derivation":"from G3474 (μωρός);","def":"silliness, i.e. absurdity","kjv":"foolishness"},"G3473":{"lemma":"μωρολογία","xlit":"mōrología","derivation":"from a compound of G3474 (μωρός) and G3004 (λέγω);","def":"silly talk, i.e. buffoonery","kjv":"foolish talking"},"G3474":{"lemma":"μωρός","xlit":"mōrós","derivation":"probably from the base of G3466 (μυστήριον);","def":"dull o